v 3
d staggeredgmm: GMM estimation of treatment effects under staggered adoption
d
d Estimates cohort-by-time average treatment effects under staggered
d treatment adoption by the generalized method of moments. Every clean 2x2
d difference-in-differences comparison (against never-treated and
d not-yet-treated units) enters an over-identified moment system that is
d combined by iterated optimal GMM, with the weight built from a model of the
d serial correlation of the errors. Three weighting schemes are provided:
d a pooled stationary covariance, a cohort-specific stationary covariance and
d an unrestricted within-cohort covariance. Optional adjustment for baseline
d covariates by outcome regression, and a serial-correlation robust
d over-identification test of parallel trends and no anticipation (estat jtest),
d are also supported. Unbalanced panels are supported.
d
d Stata implementation of the R package staggeredGMM 0.1.0 (CRAN).
d Method: Arora and Bijani (2026), doi:10.2139/ssrn.6558759.
d
d KW: difference-in-differences
d KW: staggered adoption
d KW: event study
d KW: GMM
d KW: treatment effects
d KW: parallel trends
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261030
d Homepage: https://github.com/RishabhBijani/staggeredGMM_STATA
